      "text": "Given the equation \\(7^{x+7} = 8^x\\), we aim to solve for \\(x\\). To do this, we can take the logarithm of both sides. Our goal is to express \\(x\\) in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\). Let's proceed step-by-step.\n\nFirst, we write the equation as:\n\\[7^{x+7} = 8^x.\\]\n\nBy taking the logarithm of both sides, we get:\n\\[\\log(7^{x+7}) = \\log(8^x).\\]\n\nUsing the logarithm property \\(\\log(a^b) = b \\log(a)\\), we can rewrite the equation as:\n\\[(x+7) \\log(7) = x \\log(8).\\]\n\nNext, we distribute the logarithms:\n\\[x \\log(7) + 7 \\log(7) = x \\log(8).\\]\n\nTo isolate \\(x\\), we move all terms involving \\(x\\) to one side:\n\\[x \\log(7) - x \\log(8) = -7 \\log(7).\\]\n\nFactor out \\(x\\) on the left side:\n\\[x (\\log(7) - \\log(8)) = -7 \\log(7).\\]\n\nSolve for \\(x\\) by dividing both sides by \\(\\log(7) - \\log(8)\\):\n\\[x = \\frac{-7 \\log(7)}{\\log(7) - \\log(8)}.\\]\n\nWe are given that the solution can be expressed in the form \\(x = \\log_b 7^7\\). Therefore, we need to express \\(\\log_b 7^7\\) in a similar form. Using the property of logarithms \\(\\log_b(m^n) = n \\log_b(m)\\), we have:\n\\[\\log_b (7^7) = 7 \\log_b (7).\\]\n\nWe need this to be equal to our solution for \\(x\\):\n\\[7 \\log_b (7) = \\frac{-7 \\log(7)}{\\log(7) - \\log(8)}.\\]\n\nDivide both sides by 7:\n\\[\\log_b (7) = \\frac{-\\log(7)}{\\log(7) - \\log(8)}.\\]\n\nThis implies:\n\\[\\log_b (7) = \\frac{\\log(7)}{\\log(8) - \\log(7)}.\\]\n\nBy comparing this to \\(\\log_b (7^7) = 7 \\log_b (7)\\), we can see that:\n\\[7 \\log_b (7) = \\log_b (7^7).\\]\n\nTherefore, we equate the arguments:\n\\[b^7 = 7.\\]\n\nSolving for \\(b\\), we get:\n\\[b = \\sqrt[7]{7}.\\]\n\nThe value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt[7]{7}}\\).",
