      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We have $7^{x+7} = 8^x$ which can be rewritten as $7^x \\cdot 7^7 = 8^x$. This is equivalent to $7^x \\cdot 2^7 = (2^3)^x$. Therefore, we can simplify the equation to $7^x \\cdot 2^7 = 2^{3x}$. \n\nTaking the logarithm with base 2 on both sides, we get $x \\log_2 7 + 7\\log_2 2 = 3x$. Since $\\log_2 2 = 1$, this simplifies to $x \\log_2 7 + 7 = 3x$. Moving $3x$ to the other side, we get $x (\\log_2 7 - 3) = -7$. \n\nDividing by $x (\\log_2 7 - 3)$, we find $x = \\frac{-7}{\\log_2 7 - 3}$. \n\nNow, to find $b$, we need to express $x$ in the form $x = \\log_b 7^7$. \n\nStarting from $x = \\frac{-7}{\\log_2 7 - 3}$, we want to express $x$ in terms of $\\log_b 7^7$. \n\nRecall the change of base formula: $\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_c a}{\\log_c b}$. Using this, we can rewrite $x$ as $x = \\frac{-7}{(\\log_2 7) / \\log_2 b - 3}$. \n\nTo simplify the above expression, we find a common denominator: \n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-7}{(\\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b) / \\log_2 b} = \\frac{-7 \\log_2 b}{\\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b}\n\\]\n\nNow, equating this to $x = \\log_b 7^7$:\n\n\\[\n\\log_b 7^7 = \\frac{-7 \\log_2 b}{\\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b}\n\\]\n\nUsing the property of logarithms $\\log_b a^c = c \\log_b a$, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\log_b 7^7 = 7 \\log_b 7\n\\]\n\nEquating the exponents, we have:\n\n\\[\n7 \\log_b 7 = \\frac{-7 \\log_2 b}{\\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n\\[\n7 \\log_b 7 = \\frac{-7}{\\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b}\n\\]\n\nThus:\n\n\\[\n\\log_b 7 = \\frac{-1}{\\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b}\n\\]\n\nTaking the reciprocal of both sides:\n\n\\[\nb^{\\log_b 7} = \\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b\n\\]\n\nSince $b^{\\log_b 7} = 7$, we have:\n\n\\[\n7 = \\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b\n\\]\n\nRearranging, we get:\n\n\\[\n7 = \\log_2 7 - 3 \\log_2 b \\implies \\log_2 b^3 = \\log_2 7 - 7 \\implies b^3 = \\frac{\\log_2 7}{7 - 1} = \\frac{\\log_2 7}{6}\n\\]\n\nSolving for $b$, we have:\n\n\\[\nb = \\left( \\frac{\\log_2 7}{6} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{3}}\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\nb = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{6}}}\n\\]\nor\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{6}}}\n\\]",
